      "writtenOn": "2021-06-08T21:34:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The retry conditions are a bit unclear. \n\nOld Kernel:\nr \u003c 0 \u0026\u0026 errno \u003d\u003d EAGAIN \u0026\u0026 result \u003d\u003d EC_RES_IN_PROGRESS\n\nNew Kernel:\nr \u003c 0 \u0026\u0026 errno \u003d\u003d EAGAIN \u0026\u0026 result \u003d\u003d EC_COMMAND_RESULT_UNINITIALIZED\n\nOr should we check errno \u003d\u003d EINPROGRESS on new kernel? Is it always safe to retry, if so loosening the retry condition should be ok.",
      "parentUuid": "e55bd686_a1e3e5ef",
      "revId": "c8af8d06b3082ca6730ed2039e55ab8f8ff6a873",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
